// REJECTS: Request Body should not be specified for GET end point
//
// `requestBody:` on a GET service. The grammar lists requestBody and method as independent
// optional fields of a Service in any order, and both are spelled correctly here; the
// coupling is ServiceStoreParseTreeWalker:215, which reads the already-parsed method out of
// the tree and refuses the body.
//
// Pinned because HTTP itself is ambiguous on this point -- a GET with a body is legal on the
// wire and several clients emit one -- so a rewrite has a plausible reason to allow it and no
// syntactic reason to forbid it. legend-engine forbids it at PARSE time, before any model
// exists to validate.
//
// Note the sibling constraint runs the other way and is NOT tested here: `method: POST` with
// a requestBody is fine, and that is the form in ../fixtures/t2-servicestore.pure.
###ServiceStore
ServiceStore fixture::neg::RequestBodyOnGet
(
  Service GetEmployee
  (
    path: '/employees';
    requestBody: [fixture::neg::Employee <- fixture::neg::Binding];
    method: GET;
    response: fixture::neg::Employee <- fixture::neg::Binding;
    security: [];
  )
)
